course: dictionary
lesson: 762
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word bead can mean a small ball with a hole through it, or a small round drop. Look at the clues around it.
explain: «Beads go 2 red, 3 blue, 2 red, 3 blue, 2 red, 3 blue» is about things you can thread on a string, because the colours are in a pattern. Here a bead is a small shape with a hole, like the ones in a necklace.
explain: «Beads of sweat ran down his face» is different. Sweat cannot be threaded on a string, so beads here must mean small round drops. Always ask: does this make sense with my meaning? Try swapping in your meaning and check.
fact: A bead is a small ball or shape with a hole through it, often put on a string to make a necklace or bracelet.
fact: A bead can also be a small round drop, as in «beads of sweat» or «beads of water».
fact: «A string of beads» means many beads threaded on one piece of string.
fact: «Bead pattern» means a repeating order of colours, such as red, blue, red, blue.
fact: Use the clues around the word to decide which meaning the writer means.
exercise: In «Beads go 2 red, 3 blue, 2 red, 3 blue, 2 red, 3 blue», how many groups of blue beads are there? | *3 | 5 | 2 | 9
exercise: In «Road lines are painted with special paint that has tiny glass beads in it», what are the tiny glass beads for? | To keep the paint warm | To make the paint smell nice | *To shine back the light of headlights at night | To make the lines heavier
exercise: «Beads of sweat ran down his face after the race.» What is a bead of sweat? | *A small round drop | A bracelet worn on the wrist | A long string | A cold wind
test: Ravi has 12 red beads and 18 blue beads in a pattern of 2 red, then 3 blue. How many groups of blue beads does he have? | 12 | 3 | *6 | 4
test: What is a bead? | A kind of fish | *A small ball or shape with a hole through it | A large tent for camping | A loud noise
exam: In «a string of beads», which meaning of bead fits best? | A small round drop of water | A quiet whisper | A large stone on a hill | *A small ball or shape with a hole through it
